me":"model.quality"},"link":null},{"label":"image_1","localized_name":"model.images.image_1","name":"model.images.image_1","shape":7,"type":"IMAGE","link":91},{"label":"image_2","localized_name":"model.images.image_2","name":"model.images.image_2","shape":7,"type":"IMAGE","link":null},{"label":"mask","localized_name":"model.mask","name":"model.mask","shape":7,"type":"MASK","link":null},{"localized_name":"数量","name":"n","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"n"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"种子","name":"seed","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"seed"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"图像","name":"IMAGE","type":"IMAGE","links":[88]}],"title":"[Height + Base Material] 结构与烤漆初版生成","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"OpenAIGPTImageNodeV2"},"widgets_values":["Edit the input image into a flat Color ID Map for masking.\n\nGOAL\n\nChange only the colors of the existing image regions. Preserve the original image as the exact composition and geometry reference.\n\nREGION DETECTION\n\nUse every existing closed color boundary, outline and separator in the input image to identify regions.\n\nPreserve every existing region, including small shapes, thin lines, text strokes and internal details.\n\nDo not merge, split, add, remove, move or redraw any region.\n\nTreat highlights, shadows, reflections, gradients, texture and antialiasing as appearance variations, not as new regions.\n\nCOLOR CLASSIFICATION\n\nDetermine the stable base fill color inside each existing region.\n\nColor identity includes hue, lightness and saturation.\n\nDo not group colors only because they belong to the same color family. Intentionally different dark, medium and light colors must receive different IDs.\n\nFor example, dark green, medium green, light green and cyan-green are different colors and must receive different IDs.\n\nOnly regions whose original base fill colors are genuinely the same may share an ID color. This mapping must remain consistent across the entire image, including disconnected regions.\n\nCOLOR OUTPUT\n\nReplace each region with one uniform, opaque, solid palette color.\n\nUse only these exact colors:\n\n#000000\n#FF1744\n#00E5FF\n#FFEA00\n#76FF03\n#D500F9\n#FF9100\n#2979FF\n#1DE9B6\n#AA00FF\n#C6FF00\n#FF3D00\n#00B0FF\n#64FFDA\n#E040FB\n#7C4DFF\n\nReserve #000000 for the existing background and genuine holes.\n\nAssign clearly different palette colors to adjacent regions.\n\nUse one consistent palette color for every occurrence of the same original base color.\n\nPRESERVE EXACTLY\n\nKeep the original canvas size, aspect ratio, composition, object positions, shapes, proportions, topology, boundaries, outlines, separator lines and line thicknesses.\n\nPreserve all text exactly: characters, font shape, size, spacing, position, direction and stroke geometry. Only flatten its existing fill color.\n\nDo not alter any logo, number, symbol, icon or small detail.\n\nOUTPUT\n\nReturn only the edited Color ID Map.\n\nNo gradients, shading, highlights, reflections, texture, noise, transparency changes, soft edges, glow, depth, material rendering, new outlines, labels, legend or watermark.\n\nDo not redesign or reinterpret the image. Keep everything exactly the same except the region fill colors.","gpt-image-2","1024x1024",1024,1024,"opaque","high",1,6,"randomize"],"widgets_values_named":{"prompt":"Edit the input image into a flat Color ID Map for masking.\n\nGOAL\n\nChange only the colors of the existing image regions. Preserve the original image as the exact composition and geometry reference.\n\nREGION DETECTION\n\nUse every existing closed color boundary, outline and separator in the input image to identify regions.\n\nPreserve every existing region, including small shapes, thin lines, text strokes and internal details.\n\nDo not merge, split, add, remove, move or redraw any region.\n\nTreat highlights, shadows, reflections, gradients, texture and antialiasing as appearance variations, not as new regions.\n\nCOLOR CLASSIFICATION\n\nDetermine the stable bas